course: dictionary
lesson: 6247
title: Moderately: not too little, not too much
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how much. Moderately is one of them, and it sits in the middle: not a little, not a lot. «The soup is moderately hot» means it is warm enough to eat, but not so hot that you have to wait ages.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «The talk test: if you can talk but not sing you are working moderately; if you can only gasp a few words you are working hard.» Talking but not singing is in the middle, between easy and hard, so moderately means a medium level.
explain: Moderately can also mean doing something in a sensible, controlled way. «Eat moderately» means eat enough, but not too much. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: if «a medium amount» still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: Moderately is an adverb: it tells you how much or how well something is done.
fact: «Moderately» means to a medium amount or degree; fairly but not very.
fact: «Moderately» can also mean in a sensible, controlled way, not too much: «eat moderately».
fact: «Moderately difficult» means not easy, but not very hard either.
fact: «Heat moderately» in a recipe means medium heat.
exercise: «The test was moderately difficult.» What does moderately mean here? | Impossible to finish | *Fairly difficult, but not very hard | Very easy, with no questions at all | Late, after the bell
exercise: «Please eat moderately at the party.» What does eat moderately suggest? | Do not eat anything at all | Eat as fast as you can | Eat only sweets | *Eat a sensible amount, not too much
exercise: Which word in «a moderately warm day» is the adverb that tells how warm? | *moderately | day | a | warm
test: Nadia says moderately means very hot. Why is she wrong? | It is the name of a place | *Moderately means medium, not very | Moderately means cold | Moderately means very hot, so she is right
test: «Heat the sauce moderately.» What heat does the recipe ask for? | No heat at all | Very high | *Medium heat | Freezing cold
exam: Which sentence uses moderately to mean not too much? | *Eat sweets moderately, not every day | Run as fast as you can and never stop | Sleep moderately on the sofa all day | Moderately shout across the whole room
